        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "182d41cd-7930-51b1-9435-60474de60221",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Haunted Mansion, The Greatest Game Ever Played, My Dinner with Andre, The Princess Bride, Toy Story franchise, The Incredibles, Horton Hears a Who!\n- People: Mark Frost, Wallace Shawn, Josh Flitter, Louis Malle, Harry Vardon, Francis Ouimet\n- Places: Disney theme park attraction\n- Topics: film adaptations, film roles, voice acting\n\nFacts:\n- The Haunted Mansion is a 2003 American fantasy comedy horror film based on the Disney theme park attraction of the same name.\n- My Dinner with Andre is a 1981 Louis Malle-directed comedy-drama, and Wallace Shawn played Wally Shawn in it.\n- The Princess Bride is a 1987 film, and Wallace Shawn played Vizzini in it.\n- The Greatest Game Ever Played screenplay was adapted by Mark Frost from his book The Greatest Game Ever Played: Harry Vardon, Francis Ouimet, and the Birth of Modern Golf.\n- Wallace Shawn played Ezra in The Haunted Mansion.\n- Wallace Shawn voiced Gilbert Huph in The Incredibles, which was released in 2004.\n- Josh Flitter is known for playing Eddie in The Greatest Game Ever Played and Corky in Nancy Drew.\n- Josh Flitter voiced Rudy Kangaroo in the 2008 animated film Horton Hears a Who!.\n- Wallace Shawn provided the voice of Rex in the Toy Story franchise and the voice of Calico in a 2010 film with an unspecified title.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "a0df0c8b-b9e0-56c1-a695-f1c8099ac5fe",
        "text": "Page: The Haunted Mansion (film). Sentence: The Haunted Mansion is a 2003 American fantasy comedy horror film based on the Disney theme park attraction of the same name.\nPage: The Greatest Game Ever Played. Sentence: The film's screenplay was adapted by Mark Frost from his book, \"The Greatest Game Ever Played: Harry Vardon, Francis Ouimet, and the Birth of Modern Golf\".\nPage: Wallace Shawn. Sentence: His film roles have included those of Wally Shawn in the Louis Malle-directed comedy-drama \"My Dinner with Andre\" (1981), Vizzini in \"The Princess Bride\" (1987), Ezra in \"The Haunted Mansion\", providing the voice of Rex in the \"Toy Story\" franchise, providing the voice of Gilbert Huph in \"The Incredibles\" (2004), and providing the voice of Calico in \"\" (2010).\nPage: Josh Flitter. Sentence: He is known for playing Corky in \"Nancy Drew\", Eddie in \"The Greatest Game Ever Played\", and voiced Rudy Kangaroo in the 2008 animated film \"Horton Hears a Who!",
